{"title":"Career roadmap · AI Robotics Developer","role":"AI Robotics Developer","summary":"An AI Robotics Developer combines robotics, artificial intelligence, computer vision, perception, planning, control and software engineering to build robots that can sense, understand, decide and act autonomously.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Robotics/AI intern, robotics software engineer, computer vision engineer, junior robotics developer"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"What should I specialise in?","output":"Perception, SLAM, robot learning, manipulation, navigation or autonomous systems"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Senior Robotics Engineer, Robotics AI Lead, Autonomous Systems Engineer"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How do I remain relevant?","output":"Robotics Architect, AI Robotics Lead, Autonomous Systems Architect or R&D leader"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a Robotics & Automation Engineering graduate, this is a highly aligned career. The strongest profile combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Robotics","AI/ML","Computer Vision","ROS 2","C++/Python","Control Systems"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Typical applications include autonomous mobile robots, industrial robots, warehouse robots, drones, service robots, agricultural robots, medical robotics, inspection systems and humanoid/autonomous systems."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build this","Key skills","Proof of progress"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Programming + engineering foundation"},{"text":"C++, Python, mathematics, electronics, mechanics"},{"text":"Autonomous sensor-based prototype"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Robotics fundamentals"},{"text":"Kinematics, sensors, actuators, control, embedded systems"},{"text":"Mobile/manipulator robot"}],[{"text