:"ROS 2"},{"type":"p","text":"Be comfortable with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Nodes"},{"text":"Topics"},{"text":"Services"},{"text":"Actions"},{"text":"TF2"},{"text":"Launch"},{"text":"Parameters"},{"text":"RViz"},{"text":"Simulation"}]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["PG route","Best for"],"rows":[[{"text":"M.Tech Robotics"},{"text":"General robotics"}],[{"text":"M.Tech AI/Robotics"},{"text":"AI-enabled robotics"}],[{"text":"M.Tech Artificial Intelligence"},{"text":"Robot learning/perception"}],[{"text":"M.Tech Computer Vision"},{"text":"Robot perception"}],[{"text":"M.Tech Control & Automation"},{"text":"Robot control"}],[{"text":"M.Tech Embedded Systems"},{"text":"Robot hardware/firmware"}],[{"text":"M.Tech Mechatronics"},{"text":"Integrated robotic systems"}],[{"text":"M.Tech Autonomous Systems"},{"text":"Navigation and autonomy"}],[{"text":"M.Tech Mechanical/Manufacturing"},{"text":"Industrial robotics"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential institutions include IITs, IISc, NITs and specialised research universities. Admission requirements vary by programme."},{"type":"p","text":"GATE is an important route for many Indian M.Tech programmes, but the accepted paper and eligibility should be checked for each programme."},{"type":"p","text":"GATE 2027 official portal\nCCMT\nIISc Admissions","url":"https://gate2027.iitg.ac.in/"}]},{"heading":"Study abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Country","Strong areas"],"rows":[[{"text":"USA"},{"text":"Robotics, AI, autonomous systems, robot learning"}],[{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"Robotics, automation, industrial systems"}],[{"text":"UK"},{"text":"Robotics, computer vision, autonomous systems"}],[{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"AI, robotics, perception, autonomous systems"}],[{"text":"Japan"},{"text":"Robotics, humanoids, industrial robotics"}],[{"text":"South Korea"},{"text":"Robotics, computer vision, intelligent manufacturing"}],[{"text":"Australia"},{"text":"Robotics, autonomous systems, AI"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Particularly valuable research areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Robot learning"},{"text":"Vision-language-action models"},{"text":"Humanoid robotics"},{"text":"Autonomous navigation"},{"text":"Manipulation"},{"text":"SLAM"},{"text":"Multi-agent robotics"},{"text":"Human-robot interaction"},{"text":"Sim-to-real learning"},{"text":"Medical robotics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Application pack"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"B.Tech transcript"},{"text":"CV"},{"text":"SOP"},{"text":"2–3 recommendations"},{"text":"English-language test where required"},{"text":"GitHub"},{"text":"Robotics portfolio"},{"text":"Research/project reports"},{"text":"Internship certificates"},{"text":"Publications, if available"},{"text":"Robot simulation demonstrations"},{"text":"Passport"},{"text":"Financial documents where required"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For AI robotics, demonstrate actual capability rather than simply listing “AI + Robotics” on a CV."}]},{"heading":"Career progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Robotics & Automation Student"},{"type":"h","text":"Robotics/AI Intern"},{"type":"h","text":"Junior Robotics Developer / Robotics Software Engineer"},{"type":"h","text":"AI Robotics Developer"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Robotics Engineer"},{"type":"h","text":"Robotics AI Lead / Autonomy Lead"},{"type":"h","text":"Principal Robotics Engineer"},{"type":"h","text":"Robotics Architect / Autonomous Systems Architect"},{"type":"h","text":"Robotics R&D Manager / Engineering Manager"},{"type":"h","text":"Head of Robotics / Robotics Technology Director"},{"type":"h","text":"Technical route"},{"type":"flow","items":["AI Robotics Developer","Senior Robotics Engineer","Principal Engineer","Robotics Architect","Distinguished Robotics Engineer"]},{"type":"h","text":"Research route"},{"type":"flow","items":["AI Robotics Developer","Research Engineer","Research Scientist","Senior Research Scientist","Research Lead"]},{"type":"h","text":"PhD / research directions"},{"type":"p","text":"Strong research areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Robot learning"},{"text":"Reinforcement learning"},{"text":"Imitation learning"},{"text":"Vision-language-action models"},{"text":"Humanoid robotics"},{"text":"Autonomous navigation"},{"text":"SLAM"},{"text":"3D computer vision"},{"text":"Robot perception"},{"text":"Manipulation"},{"text":"Grasp planning"},{"text":"Multi-agent robotics"},{"text":"Swarm robotics"},{"text":"Human-robot interaction"},{"text":"Sim-to-real learning"},{"text":"World models for robotics"},{"text":"Embodied AI"},{"text":"Medical robotics"},{"text":"Soft robotics"},{"text":"Autonomous drones"},{"text":"Agricultural robotics"},{"text":"Industrial robotics"}]},{"type":"note","label":"2040–2046","text":"How the role evolves"},{"type":"p","text":"The traditional robotics pipeline is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Sense","Perceive","Plan","Control","Act"]},{"type":"p","text":"AI is expanding this into:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Multimodal perception","World model","Reasoning","Task planning","Motion planning","Control","Physical action"]},{"type":"p","text":"A future AI Robotics Developer may therefore work with foundation models, multimodal AI, robot learning, simulation, digital twins and autonomous decision-making, while still needing strong robotics fundamentals."},{"type":"p","text":"The most resilient profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Robotics","AI","Perception","Planning","Control","Software Engineering"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Do not become dependent solely on an LLM or vision model. A strong AI Robotics Developer should understand what happens when the AI model is uncertain, wrong, delayed, disconnected or physically unsafe."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended final skill stack"},{"type":"flow","items":["Programming","Python","C++","Linux","Git"]},{"type":"flow","items":["Robotics","Kinematics","Dynamics","Control","Mot